course: dictionary
lesson: 6868
title: Overdue: late and still waiting
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Overdue means late. Something is overdue when it was due, or expected, by a certain time, and it has not arrived, been returned, been paid or happened yet.
explain: A library book is overdue when the day it was due back has passed and you still have it. A bill is overdue when the money has not been paid in time. «A final demand is a warning that a bill is very overdue and stronger action will follow, so acting early is easier.» Here overdue tells you the bill is late, so a warning is coming.
explain: Overdue can also mean something should have happened a long time ago, as in «a change that is long overdue». Ask yourself: what was expected, and has it not happened yet? If the answer is yes, overdue probably fits.
fact: Overdue means late: it was due by a certain time and has not arrived, happened or been done.
fact: A library book is overdue when it has not been returned by the day it was due.
fact: An overdue bill has not been paid in time.
fact: «Overdue» can mean something should have happened long ago, as in «long overdue».
fact: A baby that is overdue has not been born by the expected time.
exercise: «The library book is overdue, so it should have been back by now.» What does overdue mean? | Brand new and shiny | Lost forever in a field | *Not returned by the day it was due | Given to a friend
exercise: Nana says, «That bill is overdue, love, so pay it today.» What does overdue suggest about the bill? | It was paid early | It has a picture on it | *It has not been paid in time | It is free
exercise: In «a change that is long overdue», what does overdue mean? | It is very small | It is coming next week | It was cancelled | *It should have happened a long time ago
test: A baby that is overdue has not been born by the expected time. Which of these is an overdue bill? | *A bill that has not been paid by the time it was due | A bill that was paid on time | A bill for a new bike | A bill with a picture of a cat
test: In maths, a fee is added for each day a payment is overdue. If a payment is 3 days overdue, what does that mean? | It will be due in 3 days | *It is 3 days past the due date and still not paid | It has been paid in full | It was paid 3 days early
exam: Ella says, «My library book is overdue», and Leo says it means the book is lost. Who is right, and why? | Leo, because overdue means lost | Both are right, because overdue means lost and late | *Ella, because overdue means not returned by the day it was due | Neither, because overdue means the book is new
